<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112850" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φώρ</span></b> , ὁ, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωρός,</span> dat. pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωρσί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					9.45
				</span></i>
			:—<i>thief,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.174
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φώρ τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					334a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργεῖοι φῶρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					57
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἄνθρωποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					10.15.5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγνω δὲ φώρ τε φῶρα καὶ λύκος
				λύκον</span> prov. in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EE</u>
				1235a9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ τῶν φ. κρείττω</span> prov.
			in <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φώρτατος</span>”
				<i>most thievish,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sophr.
					1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a kind of
				<i>bee,</i> prob. <i>robber-bee,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				553b9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				625a5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωρῶν λιμήν,</span> a harbour near
			Athens, a little westward of the Piraeus, used by <i>smugglers,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				35.28
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				53
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.1.14
			</span></i>. (Like Lat. <i>fur,</i> from <i>bher-</i> (root of
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρω</span>), cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγειν καὶ φέρειν.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
